35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, the transport costs vary so much! If we go far, some people might be paying way more than others if we just use a flat fee.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"I've learned that our social bonds are fragile. Many members don't even attend the camps, and the seniors say shared living is the only way to fix it.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,We must avoid any option that requires a lottery application or self-catering. The administrative load and the daily cooking duty are far too high.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,I found out that some inland places are way too crowded! Eight people to a room? That sounds like a nightmare for sleeping!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The transport costs are volatile, and whole-building lets are risky. If we commit to a fixed price and people cancel, the club account will take the hit.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, that's exactly what I'm worried about! We need a place where the cost is stable and doesn't leave a few people paying for the ones who quit.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Ryuji, I understand the workload, but if we choose a place that's too convenient, we might miss the chance to actually bond as a club.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,Bonding is useless if the organizers are too exhausted to participate. We need a facility with a canteen and a simple booking process.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, a canteen is great, but if the rooms are tiny and crowded, everyone will be grumpy and tired! We need space to actually sleep.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,I cannot support any option with unpredictable costs. We need a destination where the price is fixed per person and doesn't rely on a total headcount.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"Maybe a local option is best? It keeps transport costs low and fair, and it's easier to manage if someone drops out at the last minute.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"But will a local option encourage the year-groups to mingle? I fear that if it's too easy to go home, the distance between members will grow.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,A local option is only viable if it doesn't require us to cook for fifty people. I will not support any plan that involves a kitchen duty.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I don't care if it's local or far, as long as we aren't crammed into one room! We need a place with proper beds and enough space.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, a local option is safer financially. The less we spend on transport and the fewer deposits we pay, the lower the risk of a deficit.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,I'm leaning towards something affordable and close. It's the only way to ensure the fee distribution is fair and doesn't punish anyone.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I'm worried about the members who don't show up. We need a destination that feels like a special event, something that makes them want to stay.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I'll support any option that is ""all-inclusive"" regarding meals and has a straightforward booking system. No lotteries, no cooking, no stress.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'm going to vote against any place that looks like a crowded dormitory. We need quality sleep to have a good training camp!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,My priority is the club's financial health. I will vote for the option that has the most predictable and lowest risk of unexpected costs.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
