60,3,1,talk,Mio,,Option A is the safest for the budget. No huge transport costs means the flat fee is fair and we don't lose money if people cancel.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,I'm afraid Option A will just be like every other day. We need the shared experience of Option B or C to bridge the gap between year-groups.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option B is out. The municipal reservation system is a nightmare of lotteries and paperwork. Option C is better because the owner handles the meals.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option B is a no-go! Those inland centres are the ones with eight people to a room. We'll all be exhausted by day three!,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Option C is a financial disaster waiting to happen. A whole-building let with a non-refundable deposit and high transport costs is too risky.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, Option C might be nice, but the transport costs for two prefectures would be huge. It would make the fee very uneven for some.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, I understand the risk, but look at the attendance sheets. If we stay on campus, the members who already feel distant simply won't come.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shizue, the organizers will be the ones paying the price for that ""experience."" Option C is the only one that removes the cooking and booking burden.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Ryuji, is the Coastal Lodge actually comfortable? If it's just another crowded dorm, I'm voting for Option A. At least we can sleep at home.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,Option A is the only choice that guarantees we won't end up with another deficit. I cannot risk the club's account on a gamble.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Mio,,"I want everyone to be happy, but I can't ignore the money. Option A is the only one where the cost is truly fair for every single member.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"If we choose Option A, we are essentially giving up on the social health of the club. We must take a risk to bring the students together.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,I cannot support Option A if it means the organizers have to manage separate accommodation for commuters. That's just more administrative work.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,"I'm really worried about the sleep quality. If Option C has private rooms or at least decent space, I'm for it. Otherwise, I'll take Option A.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Ryuji, administrative work is a temporary burden. A financial deficit is a permanent scar on the club's budget. Option A is the only responsible choice.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'll vote for Option A. It's the most balanced choice for the budget and ensures no one is unfairly burdened by the costs.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I will vote for Option C. It's the only way to create a shared environment that encourages the year-groups to actually talk and bond.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I'm voting for Option C. It's the only option that doesn't force the organizers into a cooking duty or a municipal lottery nightmare.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'll vote for Option A. I've seen what happens when people don't sleep—the training becomes useless. Campus is the safest bet for rest.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I vote for Option A. We must prioritize fiscal stability and avoid any destination that could lead to another budget shortfall.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
